    remove something material from WakeSharp Plus during a period you have paid for, you may cancel and seek
    a pro-rata refund through the store.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your calendar</h2>
  <p>
    If you enable smart alarms, you confirm you are entitled to let the app read the calendars on your
    device. WakeSharp reads them on your device only, read-only, solely to compute a wake time. See the{' '}
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Availability</h2>
  <p>
    WakeSharp runs on your device and does not need a server to ring an alarm. We do not promise the app
    will be uninterrupted or error-free, and platform changes, OS updates or device settings outside our
    control can affect it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="safety">8. Important safety notice — please read this</h2>
  <div class="callout callout--warn">
    <p>
      <strong>WakeSharp is not a medical device, a safety device, or a life-critical system. Do not rely on
      it — or on any single alarm app — as your only means of waking up for something that matters.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>WakeSharp schedules alarms through the operating system, and the operating system decides whether they sound. An alarm can fail to ring for reasons entirely outside our control, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the device being switched off, out of battery, or restarting;</li>
      <li>battery-saver, power-saving or "optimisation" settings, or the app being force-stopped;</li>
      <li>permissions being denied, revoked or changed by a system update;</li>
      <li>volume, headphones, Bluetooth routing, or a hardware fault;</li>
      <li>operating-system bugs, changes or scheduling limits; or</li>
      <li>a bug in WakeSharp itself.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>If being woken is important — a flight, an exam, a medical appointment, a shift, anything with
      real consequences — set a second, independent alarm on another device.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      The Sharpness Score is a bit of fun and a way of tracking your own mornings against your own baseline.
      It is not a clinical or cognitive assessment, it does not measure fitness to drive or work, and it must
      never be used to make a medical or safety decision. WakeSharp is not a treatment for any sleep
      condition. If you are worried about your sleep or alertness, speak to a doctor.
    </p>
  </div>

